!\"*" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 331 "Maple has very high p
recision arithmetic. However, if you push it too far, you will cause M
aple to crash or, if you are lucky, just to say, \" The object you ask
ed for is too large.\" The first of the following commands is OK but t
he second is too large to display. We will place # before them to guar
d against accidental execution. " }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }
}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 12 "#353^100000;" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 13 "#353^1000000;" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 16 "Clicking on the " }{TEXT 335 4 
"STOP" }{TEXT 334 173 " sign on the menu bar will sometimes cause Mapl
e to terminate the current computation. It depends on the type of comp
utation.  We will see examples later where it does work." }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 203 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 249 0 "" }}}{PARA 207 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
228 0 "" }}}{SECT 1 {PARA 218 "" 0 "" {TEXT 336 35 "Inserting prompts \+
and shortcut keys" }}{EXCHG {PARA 217 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 88 "You may in
sert new prompts before or after the cursor by clicking on the button \+
labeled " }{TEXT 335 2 "[>" }{TEXT 334 46 " on the menu bar or by goin
g to the menu item " }{TEXT 335 6 "Insert" }{TEXT 334 19 " and going d
own to " }{TEXT 335 15 "Execution Group" }{TEXT 334 21 " and choosing \+
either " }{TEXT 335 13 "Before Cursor" }{TEXT 334 4 " or " }{TEXT 335 
12 "After Cursor" }{TEXT 334 71 ".  If you do this a lot you may want \+
to learn the keyboard short cuts. " }}{PARA 217 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 16 "
Using Windows,  " }{TEXT 335 8 "ctrl + j" }{TEXT 334 43 " will insert \+
a prompt after the cursor and " }{TEXT 335 8 "ctrl + k" }{TEXT 334 47 
" will insert one before the cursor. (Note that " }{TEXT 335 8 "ctrl +
 j" }{TEXT 334 38 "  means to hold down the keys labeled " }{TEXT 335 
4 "ctrl" }{TEXT 334 5 " and " }{TEXT 335 1 "j" }{TEXT 334 19 " at the \+
same time.)" }}{PARA 217 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 41 "To see a list of all ke
y shortcuts go to " }{TEXT 335 18 "Help, Topic Search" }{TEXT 334 14 "
 and type in  " }{TEXT 335 13 "shortcut_keys" }{TEXT 334 92 ". Then cl
ick on the item for Macintosh, Windows or Unix depending on what compu
ter you have." }}{PARA 203 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 249 0 "" }}}}{SECT 1 
{PARA 218 "" 0 "" {TEXT 336 32 "Removing output from a worksheet" }}
{PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 89 "Sometimes one want to clear the output
 from the worksheet when it becomes too cluttered. " }}{PARA 220 "" 0 
"" {TEXT 229 1 "\n" }{TEXT 229 110 "YOU DO NOT WANT TO DO THAT NOW SIN
CE YOU WILL HAVE TO PRINT OUT THE OUTPUT IN THIS WORKSHEET FOR YOUR NO
TEBOOK" }{TEXT 334 1 "." }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}{PARA 
220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 29 "This can be done by going to " }{TEXT 335 4 
"Edit" }{TEXT 334 48 " on the menu at the top. Drag the mouse down to 
" }{TEXT 335 13 "Remove Output" }{TEXT 334 43 " and with the mouse sti
ll held down select " }{TEXT 335 16 "From Worksheet. " }{TEXT 334 68 "
When you release the mouse button all of the output will be removed." 
}}{EXCHG {PARA 203 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 249 0 "" }}}}{SECT 1 {PARA 206
