autoF'-F56-Q0&DifferentialD;F'F8F;F>F@FBFDFFFHFJFMFjnF+" }{TEXT 334 
14 " as follows. \n" }}{PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 14 "6. Then press "
 }{TEXT 335 8 "ctrl + j" }{TEXT 334 13 " or click on " }{TEXT 335 2 "[
>" }{TEXT 334 79 "  to go back into execution mode. When the cursor co
mes up type in the command " }{TEXT 226 16 "int(x^2,x=1..2);" }{TEXT 
334 45 " then execute the command by hitting return. " }}{PARA 219 "" 
0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}{PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 40 "7. To save your \+
 new worksheet go under " }{TEXT 335 4 "File" }{TEXT 334 12 " and choo
se " }{TEXT 335 4 "Save" }{TEXT 334 172 " (or click on the icon that l
ooks like a floppy disk on the menu bar). The first time you will be p
rompted to give a name. Use a single word with no spaces and end it wi
th " }{TEXT 335 5 ".mws " }{TEXT 334 4 "(or " }{TEXT 411 3 ".mw" }
{TEXT 334 17 "). For example,  " }{TEXT 335 15 "YourName01.mws " }
{TEXT 334 117 "would be a possible name for a Maple file.  If you look
 at the top of this page you will see the name of this file.  " }}
{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}{PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 95 "8. \+
If you want to start a new worksheet keeping what you already have in \+
a named worksheet use " }{TEXT 335 8 "Save As " }{TEXT 334 12 "instead
 of  " }{TEXT 335 5 "Save " }{TEXT 334 133 "and give the worksheet a n
ew name. This way you can keep your old worksheet and experiment with \+
changes without losing what you did. " }}}}{SECT 1 {PARA 218 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 336 17 "Averting disaster" }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}
{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 147 "After a worksheet has been nam
ed, you should still save it frequently by clicking on the icon of the
 floppy disk which is on the menu bar or using " }{TEXT 335 4 "Save" }
{TEXT 334 7 " under " }{TEXT 335 4 "File" }{TEXT 334 22 " or easiest: \+
pressing " }{TEXT 335 8 "ctrl + s" }{TEXT 334 136 "--to guard against \+
losing work if Maple crashes. Note that you will not need to change th
e name after you have saved it the first time. " }}}}{SECT 1 {PARA 218
 "" 0 "" {TEXT 336 35 "Using several worksheets at a time." }}{PARA 
220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 26 "Under the menu item named " }{TEXT 335 6 "Wi
ndow" }{TEXT 334 32 " you will find the four options " }{TEXT 335 41 "
Cascade, Tile, Horizontal, and Vertical. " }{TEXT 334 267 "To see the \+
effect of these first open several different worksheet in succession. \+
 An easy way to do this is just by clicking on the blank page icon on \+
the menu bar. But  you may also open any worksheets. Then select each \+
of these options. You will see what they do. \n" }}{PARA 220 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 335 28 "Cutting, Copying and Pasting" }{TEXT 334 115 ": You may \+
cut, copy and paste from a worksheet to itself or from one worksheet t
o another using the commands under " }{TEXT 335 5 "Edit " }{TEXT 334 
37 "as you would in most word processors." }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
337 0 "" }}}{SECT 1 {PARA 218 "" 0 "" {TEXT 336 21 "Maple's built-in h
elp" }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}{EXCHG {PARA 215 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 203 13 "Getting Help:" }{TEXT 201 211 " Perhaps the easiest way \+
is to use a question mark as follows: Here we suppose we forgot the co
mmand for differentiate. We guess that it is dif.  Type and execute th
e following command by hitting the Return key." }{TEXT 203 0 "" }}
{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 4 "?dif" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 215 "" 0 "" {TEXT 201 45 "This
 will bring up several options including " }{TEXT 299 4 "diff" }{TEXT 
201 1 "." }{TEXT 203 1 " " }{TEXT 201 23 " Now, you can click on " }
{TEXT 299 4 "diff" }{TEXT 201 30 " or go back and add and extra " }
{TEXT 300 1 "f" }{TEXT 201 4 " to " }{TEXT 300 4 "?dif" }{TEXT 201 
340 " and re-execute. In any event you will be led to the help page fo
r diff.  If you scroll down you will see a number of examples. This wi
ll often be enough. In some cases however you may need to read the ent
ire help page carefully. If you execute a single question mark (as fol
lows) you will bring up some general information on getting help." }
{TEXT 203 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 1 "?" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 399 "Usually you would just like to
 see some examples of how a command is used in this case. Using the do
uble question mark syntax (??) will take you to the help page of the t
opic with all of its sections contracted. Using the triple question ma
rk syntax (???) will take you the help page of the topic with the Exam
ples section (if any) expanded, and all other sections contracted. Her
e are two examples:" }}{PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 6 "??diff" }
}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 7 "???diff" }}{PARA 219 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 112 "For an
other example: Suppose that you want to know how to factor an integer \+
or a polynomial: Then you could try:" }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 
"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 7 "?factor" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 51 " Notice that the help page that comes \+
up says that " }{TEXT 335 6 "factor" }{TEXT 334 67 " is used to factor
 polynomials and not integers. It tells you that " }{TEXT 335 7 "ifact
or" }{TEXT 334 53 " is used to factor integers. Here are some examples
.\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 16 "factor(t^2-t-2);
" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "*&,&I\"tG6\"\"\"\"F&F&F&,&F$F&\"\"#!
\"\"F&" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 18 "factor(123456
789);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"**ycM7" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "
> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 20 "ifactor(123456789);\n" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "*()-I!G6\"6#\"\"$\"\"#\"\"\"-F%6#\"%.QF*-F%6#\"%2OF*" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 335 24 "Other ways to get help: " }
{TEXT 334 37 "You may do a full text search of the " }{TEXT 245 16 "Ma
ple Help Files" }{TEXT 334 13 " by going to " }{TEXT 335 4 "Help" }
{TEXT 334 34 " on the menu bar and pull down to " }{TEXT 335 17 "Full \+
Text Search " }{TEXT 334 2 "or" }{TEXT 335 14 " Topic Search." }{TEXT 
334 1 "\n" }{TEXT 334 1 "\n" }{TEXT 334 59 "Another way is to select a
 word of interest and then go to " }{TEXT 335 4 "Help" }{TEXT 334 34 "
 on the menu bar and pull down to " }{TEXT 335 17 "Help on Context. " 
}{TEXT 334 43 "Instead you may select the word and execute" }{TEXT 
335 11 " ctrl + f1." }{TEXT 334 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 203 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 249 0 "" }}}}{SECT 1 {PARA 218 "" 0 "" {TEXT 336 29 "The us
e of := , = , : , and ;" }}{EXCHG {PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}
{PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 15 "The expression " }{TEXT 335 4 "x:=2" }
{TEXT 334 54 " means \"assign 2 to the  variable x.\"  The expression 
" }{TEXT 335 5 "x:=2 " }{TEXT 334 37 "is called an \"assignment statem
ent\". " }{TEXT 337 0 "" }{TEXT 250 48 "Here are some examples: We mak
e two assignments:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 7 "x:
=2; \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 246 5 "y:=3;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"
xG6\"\"\"#" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"yG6\"\"\"$" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 45 "Now let's see what the values of x and
 y are:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 2 "x;" }}{PARA 
11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 
1 246 2 "y;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"$" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 
220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 88 "Now x is 2 and y is 3 so far as Maple is con
cerned. So if you try to solve the equation " }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Typesett
ing:-mrow(Typesetting:-mi(\"\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mi(\"
\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mi(\"\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typese
tting:-msup(Typesetting:-mi(\"x\", italic = \"true\", mathvariant = \"
italic\"), Typesetting:-mn(\"2\", mathvariant = \"normal\"), superscri
ptshift = \"0\")), Typesetting:-mo(\"+\", mathvariant = \"normal\", fe
nce = \"false\", separator = \"false\", stretchy = \"false\", symmetri
c = \"false\", largeop = \"false\", movablelimits = \"false\", accent \+
= \"false\", lspace = \"0.2222222em\", rspace = \"0.2222222em\"), Type
setting:-mi(\"x\", italic = \"true\", mathvariant = \"italic\"), Types
etting:-mo(\"+\", mathvariant = \"normal\", fence = \"false\", separat
or = \"false\", stretchy = \"false\", symmetric = \"false\", largeop =
 \"false\", movablelimits = \"false\", accent = \"false\", lspace = \"
0.2222222em\", rspace = \"0.2222222em\"), Typesetting:-mn(\"1\", mathv
ariant = \"normal\")), Typesetting:-mo(\"=\", mathvariant = \"normal\"
, fence = \"false\", separator = \"false\", stretchy = \"false\", symm
etric = \"false\", largeop = \"false\", movablelimits = \"false\", acc
ent = \"false\", lspace = \"0.2777778em\", rspace = \"0.2777778em\"), \+
Typesetting:-mn(\"0\", mathvariant = \"normal\")), Typesetting:-mi(\"
\"));" "-I%mrowG6#/I+modulenameG6\"I,TypesettingGI(_syslibGF'6%-I#miGF
$6#Q!F'-F#6&F+-F#6(F+-F#6#-I%msupGF$6%-F,6%Q\"xF'/%'italicGQ%trueF'/%,
mathvariantGQ'italicF'-I#mnGF$6$Q\"2F'/F?Q'normalF'/%1superscriptshift
GQ\"0F'-I#moGF$6-Q\"+F'FE/%&fenceGQ&falseF'/%*separatorGFP/%)stretchyG
FP/%*symmetricGFP/%(largeopGFP/%.movablelimitsGFP/%'accentGFP/%'lspace
GQ,0.2222222emF'/%'rspaceGFinF8FJ-FB6$Q\"1F'FE-FK6-Q\"=F'FEFNFQFSFUFWF
YFen/FhnQ,0.2777778emF'/F[oFco-FB6$FIFEF+" }{TEXT 334 20 "  Maple is c
onfused:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 19 "solve(x^2+x
+1=0,x);" }}{PARA 213 "" 1 "" {TEXT 458 0 "" }{HYPERLNK 458 "Warning, \+
solving for expressions other than names or functions is not recommend
ed." 4 "http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Wa
rning,%20solving%20for%20expressions%20other%20than%20names%20or%20fun
ctions%20is%20not%20recommended." "" }{TEXT 458 0 "" }}{PARA 222 "" 1 
"" {TEXT 459 0 "" }{HYPERLNK 459 "Error, (in solve) a constant is inva
lid as a variable, 2" 4 "http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/errors/
view.aspx?path=Error,%20(in%20solve)%20a%20constant%20is%20invalid%20a
s%20a%20variable,%202" "" }{TEXT 459 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 250 57 "Clearing x of the value 2 may be accomplished as follows
:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 7 "x:='x';" }}{PARA 11
 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"xG6\"F#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
250 67 "Now you see that x is just x. It no longer stands for the numb
er 2." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 2 "x;" }}{PARA 11 
"" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "I\"xG6\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 
30 "We can now solve the equation:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 19 "solve(x^2+x+1=0,x);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20
 "6$,&#\"\"\"\"\"#!\"\"*&*&F$F%^#F%F%F%)\"\"$F$F%F%,&F$F'*&,$F)F%F%F+F
%F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 16 "Note the use of " }
{TEXT 335 1 "=" }{TEXT 334 15 " as opposed to " }{TEXT 335 2 ":=" }
{TEXT 334 17 " in the equation " }{TEXT 335 15 "x^2 + x + 1 = 0" }
{TEXT 334 35 ".  We can even assign a name, say, " }{TEXT 335 4 "eqn "
 }{TEXT 334 17 "to this equation:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 15 "eqn:=x^2+x+1=0;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I
$eqnG6\"/,(*$)I\"xGF$\"\"#\"\"\"F+F)F+F+F+\"\"!" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "
> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 13 "solve(eqn,x);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6$,&#\"\"\"\"\"#!\"\"*&*&F$F%^#F%F%F%)\"\"$F$F%F%,&F$F'*&
,$F)F%F%F+F%F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 208 "We can assi
gn values to several variables at a time as in the following command. \+
Actually the parentheses in this line are not necessary, but are inclu
ded for clarity. Notice they do not appear in the output." }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 19 "(x,y,z):=(2,3,w+8);" }}{PARA 11
 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">6%I\"xG6\"I\"yGF%I\"zGF%6%\"\"#\"\"$,&I\"wGF%\"
\"\"\"\")F-" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 50 "We can see the \+
values of the variables as follows:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 6 "x,y,z;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6%\"\"#\"\"$
,&I\"wG6\"\"\"\"\"\")F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 23 "Com
pare the above with:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 9 "
x; y; z; " }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"#" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "\"\"$" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ",&I\"wG6\"\"\"\"\"
\")F%" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 12 "The command " }{TEXT 
335 9 "restart; " }{TEXT 334 74 " as noted above, is useful for cleari
ng all variables and starting afresh." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 15 "(x,y):=45,8674;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">6
$I\"xG6\"I\"yGF%6$\"#X\"%u')" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 
1 246 8 "restart;" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 4 "x,y
;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6$I\"xG6\"I\"yGF$" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 
214 "" 0 "" {TEXT 301 0 "" }}{PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 335 59 "Note that
 if a line ends with :  instead of  ; the command " }{TEXT 247 39 "is \+
executed, but the output is not show" }{TEXT 334 21 ". Here is an exam
ple:" }{TEXT 337 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 6 "
y:=14:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 2 "y;" }}{PARA 11
 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"#9" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 
246 6 "t:=12;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"tG6\"\"#7" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 69 "See what happens if you forget \+
the semi-colon at the end of the line:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 4 "t:=2" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"tG6\"\"\"#
" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 202 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 173 "You can go back to the li
ne t:=2 with the cursor and add the semi-colon or you may add it on th
e second line, where the cursor has moved to, before re-executing the \+
command." }{TEXT 460 0 "" }}}}{SECT 0 {PARA 218 "" 0 "" {TEXT 336 41 "
Functions (procedures) versus expressions" }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
337 0 "" }}{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 62 "Maple has a large nu
mber of built-in functions (also known as " }{TEXT 335 10 "procedures"
 }{TEXT 334 17 ") . For example: " }{TEXT 335 81 "sin, cos, tan, cotan
, sec, csec, arcsin, ln, exp, abs, sqrt, tan,  factorial, det" }{TEXT 
334 151 " (determinant),  and many more. These functions  behave prett
y much as you would expect. You can also make your own functions (that
 we will often call " }{TEXT 335 10 "procedures" }{TEXT 334 28 ") whic
h we illustrate below." }}{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}{PARA 202
 "" 0 "" {TEXT 250 182 "The \"obvious\" way to make a function, howeve
r, does not  work.  Suppose we want to define a new function f satisfy
ing f(x) = x^2 + x + 1 for all x. Try execute the following command." 
}}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 8 "restart;" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 15 "f(x):=x^2+x+1;\n" }}{PARA 11 ""
 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">-I\"fG6\"6#I\"xGF%,(*$)F'\"\"#\"\"\"F,F'F,F,F," }}
}{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 247 68 "This is NOT the way to do it. \+
Note what happens in the next command:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 246 5 "f(2);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "-I\"fG6\"6#\"
\"#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 10 "evalf(%);\n" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "-I\"fG6\"6#\"\"#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 220 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 334 11 "The object " }{TEXT 335 11 "x^2 + x + 1" }{TEXT 
334 22 " is what is called an " }{TEXT 335 20 "algebraic expression" }
{TEXT 334 141 ". We may plot it, solve it, factor it,  integrate it, d
ifferentiate it, and so forth, but it is NOT a function so far as Mapl
e is concerned. " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 220 "" 0 "" {TEXT 334 1 "\n" }{TEXT 
334 45 "What we would like is for f(2) to give us 7. " }{TEXT 247 54 "
Here are three correct ways to define such a function." }{TEXT 334 2 "
  " }{TEXT 247 31 "You should learn each of these." }{TEXT 334 0 "" }}
{PARA 219 "" 0 "" {TEXT 337 0 "" }}{PARA 201 "" 0 "" {TEXT 244 26 "Use
 of the arrow notation:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 
14 "f:=x->x^2+x+1;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"fG6\"f*6#I\"xG
F$F$6$I)operatorGF$I&arrowGF$F$,(*$)F'\"\"#\"\"\"F/F'F/F/F/F$F$F$" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 5 "f(2);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 ""
 {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 5 "f
(a);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ",(*$)I\"aG6\"\"\"#\"\"\"F(F%F(F(
F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 201 "" 0 "" {TEXT 244 1 "\n" }{TEXT 244 15 "Use of
 unapply:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 220 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 222 9 "restart: " 
}{TEXT 334 176 "(It is a good idea to restart after finishing one prob
lem  and starting on another. This clears the internal memory. In this
 case, it lets us clear the above definition of f. )" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 
200 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 246 22 "f:=unapply(x^2+x+1,x);" }}{PARA 11 ""
 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"fG6\"f*6#I\"xGF$F$6$I)operatorGF$I&arrowGF$F$,(
*$)F'\"\"#\"\"\"F/F'F/F/F/F$F$F$" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 200 "> " 0 "" 
